1
00:00:00,151 --> 00:00:02,991
(Sheldon:)Yeah, so the judges can give out
the prizes for best costume.

2
00:00:03,154 --> 00:00:04,904
(Sheldon:)Most frightening, most authentic...

3
00:00:05,073 --> 00:00:08,743
...most accurate visualization
of a scientific principle.

4
00:00:10,537 --> 00:00:11,997
(Penny:)Oh, Sheldon, I'm sorry...

5
00:00:12,163 --> 00:00:16,333
...but there aren't gonna be any parades
or judges or prizes.

6
00:00:17,544 --> 00:00:20,044
(Sheldon:)This party is just going to suck.

7
00:00:20,213 --> 00:00:23,003
No, come on, it's gonna be fun.
And you all look great.

8
00:00:23,174 --> 00:00:26,054
(Penny:)I mean, look at you, Thor,
and, oh, Peter Pan.

9
00:00:26,219 --> 00:00:28,299
(Penny:)That's so cute.

10
00:00:28,471 --> 00:00:31,601
- Actually, Penny, he's Robin...
- I'm Peter Pan.

11
00:00:32,350 --> 00:00:35,850
(Howard:)And I've got a handful of pixie dust
with your name on it.

12
00:00:37,397 --> 00:00:38,567
(Penny:)No, you don't.

13
00:00:41,234 --> 00:00:44,984
- Hey, what's Sheldon supposed to be?
- Oh, he's the Doppler effect.

14
00:00:45,155 --> 00:00:47,865
(Sheldon:)Yes, it's the apparent change
in the frequency of a wave...

15
00:00:48,032 --> 00:00:51,742
(Sheldon:)...caused by relative motion between
the source of the wave and the observer.

16
00:00:53,538 --> 00:00:57,288
(Penny:)Oh, sure, I see it now.
The Doppler effect.

17
00:00:57,459 --> 00:01:01,019
All right, I gotta shower. You guys,
um, make yourselves comfortable.

